      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Piquet",
          "subtitle": "Classic 2-Player",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Piquet is a classic 2-player game with 32 cards (7-A). 12 each, 8 talon. Exchange, declarations (Point, Sequence, Set), then tricks (no trump). Partie = 6 deals. Rubicon: loser <100 pays sum+100; loser â‰¥100 pays difference+100."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Piquet is one of the oldest card games still played. First mentioned as Le Cent in Rabelais (1535). Well established by 1650 with rules similar to today; early form used a 36-card pack and first to 100. Introduced in Germany during the Thirty Years' War; popular in France until the early 20th century. Spread to England after Mary I's marriage (1554), then under the French name after Charles I's marriage (1625). Cavendish codified authoritative rules in 1882."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2. Elder (non-dealer) and Younger (dealer)."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32 cards. Rank 7-8-9-10-J-Q-K-A."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32-card pack."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "12 each, 8 talon. Elder exchanges first (1-5), Younger (1 to remainder)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "style": "unordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "100 Game: First to 100 ends partie."
                },
                {
                  "text": "36-Card: 36 cards, 12 talon, elder 7 exchange."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
